  <accessrestrict id="08fbc3e4a002deca5eaf805910dbbab9">
    <head>Conditions Governing Access</head>
<p>Open for research with select materials restricted as noted. Brittle or damaged items are available at the discretion of RAC.</p>  </accessrestrict>
  <arrangement id="3976db65d7fb186c7496fe7363898776">
    <head>Arrangement</head>
<p>Arranged in three series as follows:</p><p>Series 1: John E. Craig Chronological Correspondence</p><p>Series 2: Congressional File</p><p>Series 3: Speeches and Papers</p>  </arrangement>
  <bioghist id="edead3c4859fb8cc370b995ba22be9e0">
    <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
<p>John E. Craig, Jr. served as Vice President and Treasurer of the Commonwealth Fund.</p>  </bioghist>
  <acqinfo id="7c5c585041b6d893eae11c7c8076d7ee">
    <head>Immediate Source of Acquisition</head>
<p>The Commonwealth Fund records were donated to RAC in 1985. The initial transfer of archival records to RAC began in 1986, and tranfers continue on a regular basis. These specific John E. Craig files were transferred to RAC in 2001 as accession 2001:069.</p>  </acqinfo>
  <userestrict id="df1b88e483154b27aafe33a4cf978201">
    <head>Conditions Governing Use</head>
<p>RAC has legal title, copyright and literary property rights to this collection in so far as it holds them.</p>  </userestrict>
  <scopecontent id="7bb9bd221a88e7cb9be566a2eb38bb84">
    <head>Scope and Contents</head>
<p>This set of John E. Craig files, covering the period 1975-1996, consists of incoming and outgoing correspondence, speeches, papers, and a small selection of background files pertaining to the Commonwealth Fund's congressional activities and lobbying efforts.</p>  </scopecontent>
